# Uploaded sources Vercel does not need at runtime.
#
# Deliberately conservative. Only two kinds of thing are listed:
#
#   - `node_modules`, which Vercel reinstalls from the lockfile anyway
#   - `.cache`, `coverage`, logs, and `.env`, which are local-only
#
# `scripts/` is NOT ignored even though the running service never touches it:
# `vercel.json` runs `scripts/check.sh` as the build command, and the build runs
# in the uploaded directory, so excluding it would break the deploy itself.
#
# `build/` is not ignored either. It is gitignored because it is generated on
# every deploy, not because it is unwanted in the bundle.
#
# `public/` is never ignored: the login page is read off the filesystem at
# module load, so it has to travel with the function.

node_modules
.cache
coverage
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example